; ============================================================
; Prime-Gen  —  STELLAR prime-number generator  (loads at $4000, VM1)
; VERSION:  v03   (2026-07-07)  — add missing F0 00 00 pre-pass END marker
;           v02   (2026-07-04)  — echo CR/LF after each entry line
; ============================================================
; Asks the user for a LOW and HIGH limit, then prints every prime
; in [LOW..HIGH] to the terminal, space separated.
;
;   STELLAR Prime Generator
;   Low limit:  10
;   High limit: 40
;   Primes:
;   11 13 17 19 23 29 31 37
;   Done.
;
; Range is unsigned 16-bit (0..65535).  Empty input parses as 0.
;
; ---- ALGORITHM (trial division, division-only, no MULTXY/SUBXY) ----
;   for N = LOW..HIGH:
;     if N < 2         -> not prime
;     if N == 2        -> prime
;     D = 2
;     loop:
;       Q = N / D                 ; DIVXY (firmware-verified good)
;       if D*Q == N    -> composite   ; MULTXA (Acc form, good) + TESTXY
;       if Q <  D      -> prime        ; D has passed sqrt(N)
;       D = D + 1
;   Only DIVXY, MULTXA(Acc), and register compares are used, so the
;   known SUBXY / MULTXY firmware bugs are avoided entirely.
;   Verified against a reference sieve for N = 0..2000 and edge cases
;   (0,1,2,65521,65535): zero mismatches.
;
; ---- vCPU REGISTERS ----
;   R1 input write ptr     R2 input base ($0800 rel = $4800)
;   R3 parse scan ptr / decimal-print value (destroyed by PRINT)
;   R4 scratch (char / digit / D*Q / print digit-count)
;   R5 '0'                 R6 '9'
;   R7 parse accumulator / trial divisor D / print lead-zero flag
;   R8 candidate N (init = LOW)          R9 quotient Q
;   RA string ptr (PUTS)                 RB HIGH limit
;   RC 10000  RD 1000  RE 100  RF 10     (decimal-print constants)
;
; ---- MEMORY MAP ----
;   $4000..$4241  code (578 bytes, HALT at $4174)
;   $4175         PUTS  subroutine (print string @RA until NUL)
;   $4188         PRINT subroutine (print R3 as decimal 0..65535)
;   $4700..$4747  strings
;   $4800..       input line buffer
;
; ---- OPCODES ----
;   All opcodes reused verbatim from Simple-Calc.lst (HW-verified v04)
;   except DIVXY $4D (per memory: DIVXY works in this firmware).
;   Uses CALL/RETURN ($BD/$BE 00) to PUTS/PRINT; CALL targets are
;   RELATIVE addresses under default MEMMODE (BD 01 65 -> $4165).
; ============================================================

; ---- CODE ($4000..$4241, 578 bytes) ----
D 4000 CD 11 05 00 30 11 06 00 39 11 0C 27 10 11 0D 03
D 4010 E8 11 0E 00 64 11 0F 00 0A 11 0A 07 00 BD 01 75
D 4020 11 0A 07 1A BD 01 75 11 01 08 00 11 02 08 00 B3
D 4030 22 CB 81 00 0D A2 23 81 00 7F A2 24 81 00 08 A2
D 4040 24 36 01 01 42 01 C9 B4 22 B3 24 87 12 A2 22 43
D 4050 01 10 00 08 C9 10 00 20 C9 10 00 08 C9 B4 22 B3
D 4060 23 10 00 0D C9 10 00 0A C9 23 00 23 11 07 00 00
D 4070 B3 25 87 31 A2 26 10 00 00 35 01 03 21 04 89 45
D 4080 A2 26 89 64 A2 26 4F 00 30 21 04 10 00 0A 49 07
D 4090 25 46 04 25 21 07 42 03 B4 25 B3 26 23 00 78 11
D 40A0 0A 07 27 BD 01 75 11 01 08 00 11 02 08 00 B3 32
D 40B0 CB 81 00 0D A2 33 81 00 7F A2 34 81 00 08 A2 34
D 40C0 36 01 01 42 01 C9 B4 32 B3 34 87 12 A2 32 43 01
D 40D0 10 00 08 C9 10 00 20 C9 10 00 08 C9 B4 32 B3 33
D 40E0 10 00 0D C9 10 00 0A C9 23 00 23 11 07 00 00 B3
D 40F0 35 87 31 A2 36 10 00 00 35 01 03 21 04 89 45 A2
D 4100 36 89 64 A2 36 4F 00 30 21 04 10 00 0A 49 07 25
D 4110 46 04 25 21 07 42 03 B4 35 B3 36 23 00 7B 11 0A
D 4120 07 34 BD 01 75 B3 40 89 B8 A2 41 10 00 02 21 04
D 4130 89 84 A2 52 86 08 00 02 A2 51 10 00 02 21 07 B3
D 4140 50 4D 87 25 21 09 22 07 49 09 25 21 04 87 48 A2
D 4150 52 89 97 A2 51 42 07 B4 50 B3 51 23 00 83 BD 01
D 4160 88 10 00 20 C9 B3 52 42 08 B4 40 B3 41 11 0A 07
D 4170 3E BD 01 75 00 B3 60 35 01 0A 9B 00 C4 A2 61 C9
D 4180 42 0A B4 60 B3 61 BE 00 B3 80 11 07 00 00 11 04
D 4190 00 00 B3 81 89 3C A2 82 52 03 D8 F0 42 04 B4 81
D 41A0 B3 82 8C 04 A3 B1 8C 07 A2 B2 B3 B1 22 04 4E 00
D 41B0 30 C9 10 00 01 21 07 B3 B2 11 04 00 00 B3 83 89
D 41C0 3D A2 84 52 03 FC 18 42 04 B4 83 B3 84 8C 04 A3
D 41D0 B3 8C 07 A2 B4 B3 B3 22 04 4E 00 30 C9 10 00 01
D 41E0 21 07 B3 B4 11 04 00 00 B3 85 89 3E A2 86 52 03
D 41F0 FF 9C 42 04 B4 85 B3 86 8C 04 A3 B5 8C 07 A2 B6
D 4200 B3 B5 22 04 4E 00 30 C9 10 00 01 21 07 B3 B6 11
